# issue: none
# notes: An update that rewrites whole rows carries every Blob it does not assign and counts it as `materialized blob payload bytes`; assigning a Blob (here to null) carries no payload.
# notes: The seeded payload is 2,048 bytes: write_max_bytes = 2047 refuses the carry and leaves the title old, 2048 admits it exactly.
# notes: Whether that sole update is admitted depends only on the request and the rows, never on how
# notes: it is written: an index on the assigned column (`Indexed`) or a row sharing a large fragment
# notes: under a wide assignment (`Packed`, 8,192-byte payload at 8191) would favour a row rewrite,
# notes: which does not fit, so the update patches and is admitted in both.
# notes: Nor does it depend on the rows stored beside the matched one: `Shared` holds the same 301
# notes: rows in one fragment that `Apart` holds in two (the 300 small rows appended later), and the
# notes: same sole update is admitted on both at 4096. The scan copies the matched rows out of the
# notes: decoded fragment batch before charging them; charged as a slice, `Shared` cost 7,670 bytes.
# notes: A second statement on the type keeps the update on whole rows. Alone, the same update patches the title column (issue #1264) and carries nothing, so 2047 admits it; the carry that follows is still refused at 2047, so the Blob kept its 2,048 bytes.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine
    storage: local-filesystem

--- schema
node Doc {
    slug: String @key
    content: Blob?
    title: String
}

node Indexed {
    slug: String @key
    content: Blob?
    title: String @index
}

node Packed {
    slug: String @key
    content: Blob?
    title: String
}

node Shared {
    slug: String @key
    content: Blob?
    title: String
}

node Apart {
    slug: String @key
    content: Blob?
    title: String
}

--- seed
{"type":"Doc","data":{"slug":"big","content":"base64:","title":"old"}}
{"type":"Indexed","data":{"slug":"big","content":"base64:","title":"old"}}
{"type":"Packed","data":{"slug":"big","content":"base64:","title":"old"}}
